# 必考词 Unit30
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit30核心高频词汇

{{interim}}{/ˈɪntərɪm/}}{adj. 临时的；n. 过渡期}}{{The board appointed an interim manager until a permanent replacement was found.}}

{{interplay}}{/ˈɪntərpleɪ/}}{n. 相互作用；互动}}{{The interplay between genetics and environment shapes human development.}}

{{intimate}}{/ˈɪntɪmət/}}{adj. 亲密的；私人的}}{{The couple shared an intimate moment at dinner.}}

{{intricate}}{/ˈɪntrɪkət/}}{adj. 复杂的；精细的}}{{The watch has an intricate mechanism with hundreds of parts.}}

{{intrigue}}{/ɪnˈtriːɡ/}}{v. 激起兴趣；n. 阴谋}}{{The mystery novel intrigued readers with its unexpected twists.}}

{{intrinsic}}{/ɪnˈtrɪnsɪk/}}{adj. 固有的；内在的}}{{The intrinsic value of education goes beyond monetary gains.}}

{{inventory}}{/ˈɪnvəntri/}}{n. 库存；清单}}{{The store needs to take inventory before the holiday season.}}

{{irony}}{/ˈaɪrəni/}}{n. 讽刺；反讽}}{{The irony of the situation was not lost on anyone.}}

{{irrelevant}}{/ɪˈreləvənt/}}{adj. 不相关的；不切题的}}{{Please do not include irrelevant information in the report.}}

{{isolate}}{/ˈaɪsəleɪt/}}{v. 隔离；孤立}}{{Scientists isolated the virus in a controlled laboratory environment.}}

{{jeopardize}}{/ˈdʒepərdaɪz/}}{v. 危害；使陷于危险}}{{The scandal could jeopardize his political career.}}

{{junction}}{/ˈdʒʌŋkʃn/}}{n. 交叉点；连接处}}{{Turn left at the junction ahead.}}

{{jurisdiction}}{/ˌdʒʊərɪsˈdɪkʃn/}}{n. 管辖权；司法权}}{{The case falls outside the jurisdiction of this court.}}

{{justify}}{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/}}{v. 证明...正当；为...辩护}}{{Nothing can justify such cruel behavior.}}

{{lag}}{/læɡ/}}{v. 落后；滞后}}{{Developing countries often lag behind in technology adoption.}}

{{landmark}}{/ˈlændmɑːrk/}}{n. 地标；里程碑}}{{The Supreme Court ruling was a landmark decision in civil rights.}}

{{lapse}}{/læps/}}{n. 失误；v. 终止}}{{A momentary lapse in concentration led to the error.}}

{{latent}}{/ˈleɪtnt/}}{adj. 潜在的；潜伏的}}{{The artist had a latent talent that was discovered later in life.}}

{{legitimate}}{/lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət/}}{adj. 合法的；正当的}}{{The company operates as a legitimate business entity.}}

{{levy}}{/ˈlevi/}}{v. 征收；n. 税}}{{The government levied a tax on luxury goods.}}

{{liable}}{/ˈlaɪəbl/}}{adj. 有义务的；有...倾向的}}{{The company is liable for damages caused by its products.}}

{{liberal}}{/ˈlɪbərəl/}}{adj. 自由的；开明的}}{{She holds liberal views on social issues.}}

{{linger}}{/ˈlɪŋɡər/}}{v. 逗留；徘徊}}{{The smell of cooking lingered in the kitchen for hours.}}

{{literacy}}{/ˈlɪtərəsi/}}{n. 读写能力；素养}}{{The government launched a campaign to improve literacy rates.}}

{{lobby}}{/ˈlɒbi/}}{n. 大厅；v. 游说}}{{The industry lobbied the government for favorable regulations.}}

{{lofty}}{/ˈlɒfti/}}{adj. 崇高的；高耸的}}{{She has lofty ambitions to change the world.}}

{{lure}}{/lʊər/}}{v. 诱惑；n. 诱饵}}{{The promise of high salaries lured many graduates to the city.}}

{{magnitude}}{/ˈmæɡnɪtjuːd/}}{n. 巨大；重要性}}{{The magnitude of the disaster was beyond imagination.}}

{{malicious}}{/məˈlɪʃəs/}}{adj. 恶意的；恶毒的}}{{The malicious software damaged thousands of computers.}}

{{manifest}}{/ˈmænɪfest/}}{v. 表明；adj. 明显的}}{{The symptoms of the disease may manifest in various ways.}}

{{maneuver}}{/məˈnuːvər/}}{n. 策略；v. 操作}}{{The pilot performed a difficult maneuver to avoid the storm.}}

{{marginal}}{/ˈmɑːrdʒɪnl/}}{adj. 边缘的；微不足道的}}{{The improvement was marginal and not statistically significant.}}

{{mediate}}{/ˈmiːdieɪt/}}{v. 调解；斡旋}}{{A neutral party was called in to mediate the dispute.}}

{{meritocracy}}{/ˌmerɪˈtɒkrəsi/}}{n. 精英管理；唯才是举}}{{The company promotes a culture of meritocracy.}}

{{metaphor}}{/ˈmetəfər/}}{n. 隐喻；比喻}}{{Life is often described through the metaphor of a journey.}}

{{meticulous}}{/məˈtɪkjələs/}}{adj. 一丝不苟的；细致的}}{{She is meticulous in her attention to detail.}}

{{mingle}}{/ˈmɪŋɡl/}}{v. 混合；交往}}{{Guests mingled at the reception, enjoying the festivities.}}

{{minimize}}{/ˈmɪnɪmaɪz/}}{v. 使最小化；降低}}{{The goal is to minimize the risk of errors in the process.}}

{{mobilize}}{/ˈməʊbɪlaɪz/}}{v. 动员；调动}}{{The government mobilized resources for the disaster relief effort.}}

{{momentum}}{/məˈmentəm/}}{n. 动力；势头}}{{The reform movement gained momentum across the country.}}
